# Normalise line endings.
#
# You are authoring on Windows and CI runs on ubuntu-latest. Without this, files
# committed with CRLF reach the Linux runner with trailing \r, and the failures
# are baffling: `terraform fmt -check` reports diffs it will not show you, and a
# Python file's last token on each line silently carries a \r.
#
# * text=auto keeps working copies native (CRLF locally) while storing LF in the
# repo, which is what the runner then checks out.
* text=auto

# Belt and braces for the files CI actually executes or parses.
*.tf      text eol=lf
*.hcl     text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf

# PowerShell stays CRLF - it is only ever run on Windows, and PS 5.1 is happier.
*.ps1     text eol=crlf
